---

Definition of Done (DoD)

Every feature must satisfy these criteria before completion:

Business requirements implemented

Database migrations completed

Prisma models updated

API endpoints documented

Authorization enforced

Validation with Zod

Unit tests passing

Integration tests passing

UI responsive

Accessibility checks completed

Audit logging implemented

Documentation updated

Code reviewed and merged



---

Development Standards

Every feature should include:

Prisma model(s)

Repository

Service

Validation schema

API route

Server Action (where appropriate)

React components

Loading states

Error handling

Empty states

Unit tests

Integration tests



---

Release Strategy

Alpha: Internal Aviritech team

Beta: Selected property owners, agents, and investors

Release Candidate (RC): Production-like environment with monitoring

Version 1.0: Public launch

Version 1.1+: Incremental features, AI enhancements, and integrations


The Next Step

At this point, you have the planning artifacts needed to begin implementation. The first practical deliverable should be a production-ready monorepo with:

Next.js 15 (App Router)

Clerk authentication

Prisma ORM

MySQL

Tailwind CSS

shadcn/ui

Docker

GitHub Actions

A feature-based folder structure

The repository/service architecture already wired in


From there, each sprint becomes an implementation task rather than a design exercise. That approach will keep the codebase aligned with the enterprise architecture you've defined from the beginning.
